            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "In 2018, North Carolina amended its Constitution to require photographic identification for in\u2011person voting."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "NAACP",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "86792f4b70a745703817d47d780cf8aa708a61eca0fa41b27c3df9f5dbc6584b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-86792f4b70a7-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to NAACP, the NAACP alleged that S.B.\u202f824, the voter\u2011ID law, offends the Federal Constitution."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "District Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "86792f4b70a745703817d47d780cf8aa708a61eca0fa41b27c3df9f5dbc6584b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-86792f4b70a7-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The District Court denied the legislative leaders\u2019 motion to intervene and stayed the case pending Supreme Court review."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "86792f4b70a745703817d47d780cf8aa708a61eca0fa41b27c3df9f5dbc6584b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-86792f4b70a7-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Supreme Court held that a presumption of adequate representation is inappropriate when a duly authorized state agent seeks to intervene to defend a state law."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "86792f4b70a745703817d47d780cf8aa708a61eca0fa41b27c3df9f5dbc6584b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-86792f4b70a7-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor dissented, arguing that the General Assembly\u2019s authority to defend duly enacted state statutes should be respected."
      }
    ],
